glyphfx is a port of ttfx, which is a port of TerminalTextEffects (TTE).

    TerminalTextEffects
    https://github.com/ChrisBuilds/terminaltexteffects
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 ChrisBuilds

    ttfx
    https://github.com/omacom/ttfx
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 37signals / omacom-io

Every effect in this program, the animation engine's architecture, and the
command-line interface originate with those projects. glyphfx is an
independent C17 implementation of the same behavior; it is a parity port and
adds no art of its own. The behavior is specified against the ttfx binary and,
through it, the TerminalTextEffects design.

The parity test suite compares glyphfx byte for byte against the ttfx binary.
ttfx is not vendored here; tools/parity/fetch_reference.sh clones it on demand.

If you enjoy these effects, the credit belongs upstream.
